course: dictionary
lesson: 6906
title: Science words: oxalic acid
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some science words name a substance, and «oxalic» is one of them. In oxalic acid, the word «oxalic» describes which kind of acid it is. The whole name is the important part.
explain: Read the words around it to work out what it means. «Rhubarb stalks are safe to eat cooked, but rhubarb leaves are poisonous because they contain a lot of oxalic acid.» The word «but» shows a contrast: the stalks are safe, the leaves are not. The reason given is the oxalic acid, so it must be the poisonous part.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Rhubarb leaves are poisonous because they contain a lot of poisonous acid» still makes sense, so you have the right idea. Oxalic acid is also used for cleaning and bleaching, so it is not only found in plants.
fact: Oxalic acid is a poisonous acid.
fact: It is found in small amounts in plants such as rhubarb leaves, sorrel and spinach.
fact: Rhubarb stalks are safe to eat cooked, but rhubarb leaves are poisonous.
fact: Oxalic acid is used for cleaning and bleaching, and in chemistry it removes rust and stains.
exercise: «Rhubarb stalks are safe to eat cooked, but rhubarb leaves are poisonous.» Which part of rhubarb is poisonous? | The stalks when cooked | The sugar | *The leaves | Cooking the plant
exercise: Which of these plants contains oxalic acid? | *Spinach | Sugar | Castle | Copper
exercise: Oxalic acid is used for which job? | Lighting the classroom | Making rain | *Removing rust and stains | Baking cakes
test: In «rhubarb leaves are poisonous because they contain a lot of oxalic acid», what does the word «because» tell you? | *It gives the reason | It ends the sentence | It shows a place | It names a colour
test: What is oxalic acid used for in chemistry? | *Removing rust and stains | Making bread rise | Cooking rice | Watering plants
exam: Sam says «oxalic» is a type of plant. What is the best answer? | No, it is a kind of rust | *No, oxalic is an adjective that describes an acid, such as oxalic acid | Yes, it is a kind of spinach | Yes, it is a leaf found on rhubarb
